    "media:imagetext": "DO NOT OPERATE THE FOLLOWING WHILE ABOARD THE AIRCRAFT\nNO SMOKING\nRadios\nVisible Fluid Lighters\nElectric Computers\nFASTEN SEAT BELT\nIt is recommended that you\nkeep your Seat Belt\nLavatory\nEVACUATION ON WATER\nThere are eight (8) 25-MAN LIFE RAFTS located in compartments\nwithin the aircraft cabin marked:\n\"LIFE RAFT\"\nTwo (2) LIFE RAFTS\nare stowed in the forward\nceiling compartments.\nFour (4) LIFE RAFTS\nare stowed in the mid cabin\nceiling compartments.\nTwo (2) LIFE RAFTS\nare stowed in the aft\nceiling compartments.\nfastened at all\ntimes while seated\nFasten\nBEFORE TAKEOFF AND LANDING\nSeat back up\nUnfasten '\nBRACE POSITIONS\nEMERGENCY LANDING/DITCHING\nTray table up\nEach 25-MAN LIFE RAFT weighs approximately\n130Ibs. and should be removed by two able-bodied\npersons, carried to an EXIT, and secured to the aircraft\nprior to launching.\nCarry-on\nbaggage under\nseat\nAUTOMATIC OXYGEN SYSTEM\nNO SMOKING\n1. Stand beside the\ncompartment and\npull release latch\nmarked \"LIFE RAFT\"\ntowards floor. Allow\ncompartment door\nto swing open\ntowards floor.\nLIFE RAFT INFLATION\n1. OXYGEN MASK LOCATION\nOxygen masks are stored in\na compartment above each\nrow of passenger seats.\nShould oxygen be required,\nthe compartment door\nwill open automatically\nand oxygen masks will\nbe presented on the door.\n2. USING THE MASK\nShould oxygen masks appear,\nremain seated. Grasp nearest\nmask and remove it from its\nholder, at the same time pulling free the cord connect-\ning mask to the compartment. This will permit the\noxygen to flow. Place mask over nose and mouth and\nbreathe normally. Continue to use oxygen until other-\nwise directed by a crew member.\n3. ADJUSTING THE\nMASK\nThe oxygen mask has an\nadjustable head strap to\nprovide a comfortable fit.\nIf mask is too tight, hold mask in position and pul\ngently on headband with free hand. If mask is toc\nloose, pull tabs located where headband connects\nto oxygen mask.\nBORMAL\nCAPACITY\n25 PERSONS\n2. Grab assist\nstraps at fore\nand aft end of raft\nand lower to floor.\nClose ceiling\ncompartment.\nA. Unsnap RED pouch marked \"LANYARD CORD\" and\nsecure spring snap at end of cord to seat leg, fastened\nseat belt or exposed door hinge nearest the exit.\n8. Position LIFE RAFT on exit threshold and\nunsnap HOT-PINK flap containing inflation\nhandle. Grasp this handle and pull hard as\nyou push LIFE RAFT out of aircraft.\nLIFE RAFT will inflate in approximately\n15 seconds.\nWARNING!\nDO NOT INFLATE LIFE RAFT INSIDE AIRCRAFT.",
